      "status": "passed_source_review",
      "findings": [
        "The exact square-coupled oscillator Hamiltonian includes the fixed frequency counterterm. Its Drude spectral density gives the stated causal susceptibility.",
        "The completed source retains full thermal position and momentum covariances, including quantum fluctuations and finite reservoir cutoff. Its derivative of bare oscillator energy is mathematically correct but differs from the sample-minus-blank calorimeter readout at finite coupling.",
        "Subtracting the two finite-device heat inputs before taking the continuum limit defines a finite observable. The independent reference diagonalizes both finite bath Hamiltonians; it does not reuse the source susceptibility or oracle spectral-shift derivative.",
        "An independent Matsubara partition product, differentiated with complex Drude roots and a trigamma recurrence, confirms the continuum oracle and its isolated-oscillator, low-temperature and classical limits.",
        "Public initial equilibrium, complete Hamiltonian, temperature protocol, matched blank, limit order and fixed controls determine the calorimeter response without giving a spectral-shift or reduced-partition formula."
